# Framework-owned .gitignore — ignores ONLY local/ephemeral cruft.
#
# It deliberately does NOT ignore your content. A private (checked-out) instance versions its full
# history: populated registries, per-client workspaces, and generated output/ and state.md are all
# tracked, for durability and history. "Public stays empty of client content" is enforced by
# scripts/check-no-content.sh in CI (docs/operating-model.md), NOT by this file.
#
# NOTE: Graphify graphs do NOT live in this repo. They live in each client repo's local checkout
# (graphify-out/, gitignored there) and are read by path. Nothing graph-related is stored here.
#
# state.md is derived from the tracking spreadsheet (the SSOT) but is still tracked in your
# instance for history. The spreadsheet remains authoritative on any disagreement.

# Cloned OSS reference repos consulted when authoring agents/skills — license-separate,
# never committed into this MIT framework. See docs/agents-and-skills-sourcing.md.
/reference/

# OS / editor / local cruft.
.DS_Store
*.local.*
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python bytecode caches (plan step 21; step-7 carry-forward RV-2).
__pycache__/

# Per-user instance workspaces: EVERYTHING under users/<owner>/zones/<zone>/workspaces/<ws>/ is
# client/ instance data — topics, sources, defaults, generated artifacts/deliverables/reviews/
# outlines/assets/ssot, AND the transient claims/lease + async job/idempotency runtime records
# (design §13.3/§22.3/§22.7/§23). NEVER tracked in the public framework (CLAUDE.md rules 2/4);
# check-no-content.sh fails on any tracked users/*/… file — the loud backstop for a force-add.
# Broadly ignorable now that the shared blueprint lives at templates/workspace/, not among the
# workspaces (pre-restructure the tracked template forced per-subdir ignores here).
# BOTH patterns are kept ADDITIVELY (Z5, the zone restructure): `users/*/zones/` covers the
# post-migration zoned layout, and `users/*/workspaces/` still covers the pre-migration layout —
# so a downstream that pulls this update BEFORE running migrate-to-zones-layout.sh never has its
# existing client content un-ignored (there is no un-ignore window; the old pattern is harmless
# post-migration since nothing matches it once workspaces/ dirs move under zones/).
users/*/workspaces/
users/*/zones/

# Instance-scoped ops state (design §22.5/§23; plan step 36): the presence-lease registry
# and the append-only telemetry JSONL. Framework MECHANISM (pipeline/telemetry.py), instance
# DATA — CONTENT-FREE (counts/timings only) yet still instance-local, never tracked in the
# public framework (CLAUDE.md rule 4; check-no-content.sh flags any tracked instance/ops/ file).
instance/ops/

# DR-1 HTTP shim per-deployment config (Commit 5b): the auth SECRET set + the DoS caps. Framework
# MECHANISM (pipeline/api/http_shim.py + instance/shim.template.yaml, which SHIPS), instance DATA —
# the populated file holds the auth secret and is NEVER tracked in the public framework (CLAUDE.md
# rule 4; check-no-content.sh flags a tracked non-template instance/ file). Only the template ships.
instance/shim.yaml
